# .railwayignore — what `railway up` must NOT upload.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS (6 Aug). Every `railway up` archives the working tree and ships it to
# Railway's snapshot endpoint — once PER SERVICE, so one `ship.sh` run uploads the repo FOUR
# times. The tracked tree is ~137MB, and Railway's ingest intermittently times out on it:
# "Failed to create code snapshot. Please review your last commit, or try again." — which
# reads like a git problem and is actually a payload problem. Two deploys failed this way on
# 6 Aug alone (portal, website), each silently leaving the OLD version serving.
#
# `docs/` is 25MB of that and NO deploy has ever needed it — docs don't deploy (CLAUDE.md:
# "Docs don't deploy → no preview needed"). Cutting it saves ~100MB per ship.
#
# ⚠️ WHAT MUST NEVER GO IN HERE: anything a BUILD reads. `packages/` (both apps import
# @kind/shared), `supabase/` (small, and pending-migrations.ts cites its files), app assets
# (`apps/website`'s 65MB of images ARE the website). When a deploy breaks mysteriously after
# an edit to this file, this file is the first suspect.
#
# (`node_modules` and build output are already excluded via .gitignore, which the Railway
# CLI also respects. `.git` is never uploaded.)

docs/
.github/
